a priority, okay?

45:38.239 --> 45:41.539
No. No, they're
pulling our leg, man.

45:42.645 --> 45:45.180
Oh. Mmm-hmm.

45:46.580 --> 45:48.983
Yeah, that's 'cause
they're in real estate, Jason.

45:49.085 --> 45:50.281
All right, look.
Uh, I gotta bounce.

45:50.383 --> 45:52.158
I will hit you back later,
all right?

45:52.260 --> 45:53.354
All right, peace.

45:53.456 --> 45:58.561
Whoo! I just get so fricken
hyped on first Sundays, right?

45:58.663 --> 45:59.929
-Oh, come on.
-Oh.

46:00.031 --> 46:01.667
Ben Johnson,
 Midwest Christian Magazine.

46:01.769 --> 46:04.169
Oh, come on.
I know who you are. Please.

46:04.271 --> 46:05.936
Have a seat.

46:06.038 --> 46:07.867
Look, I'm sorry we couldn't
sit down last month.

46:07.969 --> 46:09.370
I was actually in Korea.

46:09.472 --> 46:10.905
We're opening a church over
there, so it's exciting stuff.

46:11.007 --> 46:12.904
-Korea?
-It's a magical place.

46:13.006 --> 46:14.305
Magical people.

46:14.407 --> 46:17.913
Complicated tax laws, so...
(CHUCKLES)

46:18.015 --> 46:19.484
I think our readers
just want to know

46:19.586 --> 46:20.545
the man behind the movement.

46:21.684 --> 46:22.814
Let's do it!

46:22.916 --> 46:23.886
Let's do it.

46:23.988 --> 46:25.324
Uh, you want to start
with the photos?

46:25.426 --> 46:26.824
-Sure. Yeah.
-Um...

46:26.926 --> 46:28.256
Can you tell me about
this one right here?

46:28.358 --> 46:31.259
Okay. Uh, that's me
and the President of Armenia.

46:31.361 --> 46:33.193
President of Panama. Look,
the church has been lucky

46:33.295 --> 46:34.993
to make some good friends
over the years.

46:35.095 --> 46:37.768
That is me with El Chapo.

46:37.870 --> 46:40.504
Super interesting dude
if you actually,

46:40.606 --> 46:42.340
I don't know, talk to him.

46:42.442 --> 46:43.467
I mean... (CHUCKLES)

46:43.569 --> 46:46.777
But the press barbequed me
for that one too.

46:46.879 --> 46:48.177
I'm not sure
if you know this, but...

46:49.509 --> 46:52.478
I'm from like a, kind of
a well-known family.

46:53.987 --> 46:55.013
I don't know. It just means
people are always

46:55.115 --> 46:56.049
trying to knock me down.

46:56.151 --> 46:57.653
You know,
take me out the game.

46:57.755 --> 46:59.083
I just always tell myself

46:59.185 --> 47:00.119
it's nothing my buddy J.C.

47:00.221 --> 47:01.658
didn't have
to deal with, right?

47:01.760 --> 47:03.122
It's, like, don't hate on me

47:03.224 --> 47:04.725
just 'cause
my dad's a big deal,

47:04.827 --> 47:06.098
or whatever, right?

47:06.200 --> 47:07.162
Amen.

47:07.264 --> 47:08.960
STEVEN: Yeah, you get it.
You know who else got it?

47:09.062 --> 47:10.632
Mayor of Kyoto.

47:11.335 --> 47:13.372
God put it on my heart
to open a church there, too.

47:13.474 --> 47:14.772
And he gave me this. Oh.

47:14.874 --> 47:15.969
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)
Look at that.

47:16.071 --> 47:17.168
(STEVEN MIMICS SWORD SWISHING)

47:17.270 --> 47:19.043
Whoa, whoa, whoa. (CHUCKLES)

47:20.208 --> 47:22.079
-Ooh-ah!
-(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

47:22.181 --> 47:24.609
Here, feel it. Feel the tip.
Feel how sharp that is.

47:26.314 --> 47:27.551
Feel it. Come on.
You gotta feel it.

47:27.653 --> 47:28.684
Okay. (CLEARS THROAT)

47:28.786 --> 47:29.887
That's it, just touch it.

47:29.989 --> 47:32.516
-Wow. Ow. (CHUCKLES)
-STEVEN: Right? (LAUGHS)

47:32.619 --> 47:34.621
STEVEN: Yeah, it's, like,
razor sharp, right?

47:34.723 --> 47:36.061
So sharp.

47:36.163 --> 47:37.663
I can give you a shave from
all the way over here, right?

47:37.765 --> 47:39.426
Well, I shaved
this morning, so...

47:43.932 --> 47:45.135
I know it was you.

47:48.437 --> 47:50.007
I knew it was you
before you walked in the door.

47:50.109 --> 47:52.505
See, Ben Johnson retired
eight months ago, so...

47:54.145 --> 47:55.339
Your other victims
might've been too dumb

47:55.441 --> 47:57.510
to put it together,
but not me.

47:58.579 --> 48:00.348
You don't get out of here
until you come clean.

48:02.390 --> 48:03.381
Come clean? What?

48:03.483 --> 48:04.955
STEVEN: Come on.
Come on, let me hear it.

48:05.057 --> 48:06.391
BECKET: Hear what?
What... what do you want?

48:06.493 --> 48:08.391
The truth. Come on.

48:08.927 --> 48:10.193
You gotta
let that shit out. Right?

48:10.295 --> 48:11.796
Look, I think you have me
confused with someone else.

48:11.898 --> 48:13.898
-I know everything! Say it!
-(YELPS)

48:14.000 --> 48:15.064
(HESITATES)
What do you want me to say?

48:15.167 --> 48:16.330
-What do you want me to say?
-Give it to me!

48:16.432 --> 48:18.596
-Come on! Come on!
-Hey! Okay, okay, okay, okay.

48:18.698 --> 48:21.202
Get it out there in the air.
Exorcise that shit!

48:21.304 --> 48:22.635
Okay, okay, okay.
I lied. I lied. I lied.

48:22.737 --> 48:24.776
-I'm not Ben Johnson. Okay.
-STEVEN: You're not, are you?

48:24.878 --> 48:26.137
-Who are you?
-I'm Becket. I'm Becket.

48:26.239 --> 48:27.878
I'm... I'm your cousin!

48:27.980 --> 48:29.509
(UPBEAT MUSIC
PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS)

48:33.915 --> 48:35.112
(MUSIC STOPS)

48:35.214 --> 48:36.417
What'd you just say?

48:37.787 --> 48:38.958
I'm your...

48:39.857 --> 48:41.059
I'm... I'm your cousin.

48:42.662 --> 48:44.256
You're not from The Post?

48:44.358 --> 48:45.496
You're not
writing a hit piece?

48:45.598 --> 48:46.592
You're not that guy?

48:49.831 --> 48:50.970
What?

48:53.669 --> 48:54.633
Oh.

48:55.840 --> 48:58.975
(LAUGHS AWKWARDLY) Okay.

48:59.077 --> 49:02.210
Uh, this is embarrassing.
(CHUCKLES)

49:02.313 --> 49:05.449
I just get so paranoid
with this job, you know?

49:05.551 --> 49:07.382
It's... Whew!

49:07.849 --> 49:08.952
Whew!

49:09.054 --> 49:11.955
Oh, man. I shoulda known
we were family.

49:12.057 --> 49:13.553
It's like looking
in a freakin' mirror.

49:14.428 --> 49:16.424
(SLURPING)

49:17.790 --> 49:19.757
(EXHALES) Something's
a little off with that.

49:21.530 --> 49:23.766
BECKET: Did you know
 that tropane alkaloids

49:23.868 --> 49:24.836
 are an active ingredient

49:24.938 --> 49:26.698
 in most pre-workout
 supplements?

49:28.073 --> 49:29.138
 If you have
 too much of the stuff,

49:29.240 --> 49:30.768
 you might have
 a massive heart attack.

49:31.577 --> 49:32.672
(BELL TOLLS)

49:32.774 --> 49:36.313
BECKET: And by too much,
 I mean about 1,500 milligrams.

49:36.415 --> 49:40.685
And the last thing the church
wanted was an investigation.

49:40.788 --> 49:42.483
I'm sure
you know all about that.

49:43.720 --> 49:45.349
Anyway...

49:45.451 --> 49:47.620
(POIGNANT PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)

49:49.896 --> 49:52.295
 Finally,
 I was getting somewhere.

49:55.095 --> 49:56.266
 Wasn't I?

49:57.630 --> 50:00.798
MARY: Promise me
 that you won't quit.

50:02.769 --> 50:05.803
 Not until you have
 the right kind of life.

50:08.013 --> 50:10.148
(POIGNANT PIANO MUSIC
CONTINUES)

50:29.436 --> 50:30.229
(LAUGHS)

50:30.331 --> 50:31.532
RUTH: Can you keep a secret?

50:33.534 --> 50:35.404
BECKET: Surprisingly well,
actually.

50:37.210 --> 50:39.408
I was gonna break up with him
that weekend.

50:42.079 --> 50:43.882
And now he's gone, and I know

50:43.984 --> 50:46.181
I'm supposed to feel,
like, devastated

50:46.283 --> 50:48.579
but I... I don't...
I don't. (SIGHS)

50:48.681 --> 50:52.751
No. You feel what
you're supposed to feel.

50:55.963 --> 50:57.823
Does that make me
a terrible person?

50:57.925 --> 50:59.164
No.

51:00.130 --> 51:01.562
I think it makes you honest.

51:05.469 --> 51:07.533
I don't know. I think
I'm still going to hell.

51:07.635 --> 51:09.608
-(CHUCKLES)
-Man, you're talking to a guy

51:09.710 --> 51:10.469
who works on Wall Street.

51:10.571 --> 51:13.307
RUTH: Oh, you're
definitely going to hell.

51:13.409 --> 51:15.007
Do you want to grab dinner
this week?

51:15.109 --> 51:17.215
Yes. (LAUGHS)

51:17.317 --> 51:20.179
Um, my office can grab us
a reservation at The Modern.

51:20.281 --> 51:22.548
Uh, it's midtown. Um...

51:22.651 --> 51:24.587
I've never been there,
but I hear it's great.

51:24.689 --> 51:26.091
Yeah.

51:26.193 --> 51:30.525
Or we could keep it simple
and cook something?

51:32.030 --> 51:34.496
Yeah, simple. I love simple.

51:48.714 --> 51:49.874
(MUSIC STOPS)

51:50.749 --> 51:51.711
(BECKET EXHALES)

51:52.412 --> 51:54.817
I know. Dramatic, right?

51:54.919 --> 51:55.885
What are you doing?

51:55.987 --> 51:57.322
JULIA: What are you doing?

51:57.757 --> 51:59.288
We had an agreement.

51:59.390 --> 52:01.960
First off, how did you
get in my apartment?

52:02.062 --> 52:03.657
I took a key
right in front of you.

52:04.324 --> 52:05.827
No, I remember.

52:06.363 --> 52:09.894
Two calls, two emails,
nothing back?

52:11.071 --> 52:12.699
-I've been occupied.
-JULIA: With what?

52:13.871 --> 52:14.833
Occupations.

52:17.104 --> 52:18.276
Go on.

52:25.750 --> 52:27.282
Come on.

52:27.384 --> 52:29.317
How long have
we known each other?

52:29.419 --> 52:30.789
-Quite some time.
-JULIA: So you should

52:30.891 --> 52:31.916
be able to tell me anything.

52:33.187 --> 52:34.358
I'll go first.

52:35.157 --> 52:36.158
We're flat broke.

52:36.260 --> 52:37.158
My husband
lied to me for years,

52:37.260 --> 52:38.857
and he's an absolute coward.

52:39.666 --> 52:41.063
Now you go.

52:41.165 --> 52:42.700
I have nothing to tell you.

52:42.802 --> 52:43.763
I would never judge.

52:44.969 --> 52:45.930
BECKET: For what?

52:57.747 --> 53:00.549
Well, that would sour things
between us, wouldn't it?

53:04.088 --> 53:05.290
I don't like it sour.

53:08.420 --> 53:09.591
I like it sweet.

53:10.697 --> 53:11.791
(DOORBELL RINGS)

53:13.828 --> 53:15.559
Oh, my God. Julia. I'm s...
(CLEARS THROAT)

53:15.662 --> 53:16.969
-JULIA: What?
-You have to go.

53:17.071 --> 53:18.169
JULIA: Are you
fucking kidding me?

53:18.272 --> 53:19.570
-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
-JULIA: What the hell?

53:19.673 --> 53:20.668
I'm sorry.

53:21.972 --> 53:22.901
You've gotta go.

53:29.210 --> 53:30.942
-Hey.
-Hi.

53:32.615 --> 53:35.252
It's a bit of a culinary
disaster in there.

53:35.355 --> 53:39.650
Oh. Uh, oh, no. (LAUGHS)
Everything okay or...?

53:39.752 --> 53:41.725
Uh, do you want
to go out to eat?

53:41.827 --> 53:42.791
Yeah, sure.

53:42.893 --> 53:43.823
Great.

53:45.325 --> 53:46.625
(RUTH LAUGHS)

53:46.727 --> 53:48.898
These students,
I love them, but...

53:49.000 --> 53:49.794
Tell me about it.

53:49.896 --> 53:51.168
RUTH: They all want
to be millionaires,

53:51.270 --> 53:54.172
but none of them
want an actual job.

53:54.274 --> 53:56.072
BECKET: They all gotta
have a dream, right?

53:56.175 --> 53:58.574
-I get it, but...
-Thank you.

53:58.976 --> 54:00.378
Thank you.

54:03.983 --> 54:04.943
I mean, I think it's...

54:05.745 --> 54:07.484
I think it's good
to want more.

54:08.416 --> 54:10.783
Okay, gun to your head.

54:10.885 --> 54:12.617
What would you even do
with a billion dollars?

54:12.719 --> 54:13.923
Why do you have
a gun to my head?

54:14.025 --> 54:14.785
Answer the question.

54:14.887 --> 54:16.587
Get those chopstick guns
out of my face.

54:16.689 --> 54:18.226
(LAUGHS) Answer the question.

54:18.329 --> 54:19.826
-I don't know.
-(RUTH CHUCKLES)

54:22.334 --> 54:23.796
I'd take you
to a better restaurant.

54:23.898 --> 54:28.906
Working in fashion
was my lifelong goal, right?

54:29.008 --> 54:30.738
Like, I had tunnel vision.

54:30.840 --> 54:35.246
And now all I can think about
is the time I put in.

54:35.348 --> 54:39.349
What, uh, we shouldn't
chase what we want?

54:39.452 --> 54:42.384
The thing is,
I think I knew the whole time.

54:42.486 --> 54:44.653
-Knew what?
-That I didn't like it.

54:45.688 --> 54:48.124
That I might be happier
making shit money

54:48.226 --> 54:50.428
and having a cactus garden.

54:52.759 --> 54:56.027
It's just scary
to dream small.

54:57.434 --> 54:59.096
Nobody teaches us
how to do that.

55:01.603 --> 55:02.668
FATHER MORRIS: Uh, sorry, I...

55:02.770 --> 55:04.140
 I don't mean
 to interrupt, but...

55:04.243 --> 55:06.477
at this point,
you met someone,

55:07.211 --> 55:08.479
you had a good career.

55:09.179 --> 55:10.712
Was that not enough?

55:12.181 --> 55:13.352
Enough what?

55:18.725 --> 55:19.787
Look...

55:21.093 --> 55:22.425
 It wasn't lost on me.

55:22.527 --> 55:25.160
 I had a good job,
 a budding romance.

55:25.262 --> 55:26.497
 Maybe I should hit pause

55:26.599 --> 55:29.496
 on the systematic killing
 of my entire family.

55:29.598 --> 55:31.430
Reservation at Manilla's,
Friday?

55:31.532 --> 55:33.136
Friday? Get outta here.

55:33.238 --> 55:34.269
-(VOICEMAIL BEEPS)
-No way.

55:34.371 --> 55:35.338
JULIA: Becket, it's me again.

55:35.440 --> 55:37.175
 And you're not answering...
 again.

55:37.277 --> 55:38.605
 I wouldn't ignore me
 much longer.

55:38.707 --> 55:40.772
 Something bad might happen,
muchacho.

55:40.874 --> 55:42.239
BECKET: But how
 could I quit now?

55:42.341 --> 55:45.945
 I mean, not even one had been
 investigated as a murder.

55:46.854 --> 55:47.947
 Was I that good?

55:49.550 --> 55:51.055
 Maybe I was that good.

55:51.157 --> 55:52.049
 Of course, by this point,

55:52.151 --> 55:54.357
 the family had realized
 that something was up.

55:54.459 --> 55:55.586
-(CHILDREN LAUGHING)
-INTERVIEWER: CEO.

55:55.688 --> 55:57.557
And now, adoption icon.

55:57.659 --> 55:59.026
BECKET:
 Take my Aunt Cassandra.

55:59.128 --> 56:01.692
 She had gotten sort of famous
 for adopting, like, 11 kids

56:01.794 --> 56:03.128
 from 11 different countries

56:03.230 --> 56:05.397
 and they spoke 11 different
 languages around the house.

56:05.499 --> 56:06.701
(CHILDREN CLAMORING)

56:06.803 --> 56:10.171
Okay, I am on the phone.
We can see that, right?

56:10.273 --> 56:11.541
Do we know phone,

56:11.643 --> 56:13.709
or do I need to tattoo it
on my fucking forehead?

56:13.811 --> 56:15.413
BECKET: She heard about
 the deaths in the family

56:15.515 --> 56:17.543
 and got a laser-based security
 system installed

56:17.645 --> 56:19.613
 in all four of her houses.

56:19.715 --> 56:21.286
 But there wasn't
 a security system

56:21.388 --> 56:23.354
 at the Blessings
 of the Desert Day Spa

56:23.456 --> 56:25.583
 where she spent
 every Tuesday afternoon.

56:25.685 --> 56:26.854
I'm sorry to disturb you.

56:26.956 --> 56:29.755
We're offering complimentary
teeth whitening services

56:29.857 --> 56:32.527
until 5 o'clock,
if you're interested.

56:32.629 --> 56:34.727
I have some literature
on the process,

56:34.829 --> 56:35.794
safety information,
if you'd like.

56:35.896 --> 56:37.161
CASSANDRA: I didn't
come here to read.

56:41.138 --> 56:42.440
Blessings.

56:42.542 --> 56:45.772
 The special ingredient
 was carbamide peroxide

56:45.874 --> 56:47.242
 which is so close
 to the acidic agent

56:47.344 --> 56:48.479
 found in teeth whitener

56:48.581 --> 56:49.947
 that the police thought
 she must have bought

56:50.049 --> 56:50.943
 an off-brand batch

56:51.045 --> 56:53.150
 during her last adoption trip
 to Cambodia.

56:53.252 --> 56:55.080
(CASSANDRA SPEAKING, MUFFLED)

56:55.915 --> 56:58.649
-(BELL TOLLS)
-(DUCKS QUACKING)

56:58.751 --> 57:00.954
(CELL PHONE VIBRATES)

57:05.663 --> 57:06.990
BECKET: Then there's
 my Uncle McArthur.

57:07.092 --> 57:08.794
Sir, you've got about
a 30-knot wind

57:08.896 --> 57:10.565
coming out
of the north-northwest.

57:10.667 --> 57:11.830
-Just so you know.
-Thanks, but I think

57:11.932 --> 57:14.303
I can handle
some goddamn wind, chief.

57:14.406 --> 57:15.538
BECKET: This guy owned, like,

57:15.641 --> 57:17.309
 half The National Air
 and Space Museum.

57:17.411 --> 57:18.802
 And while the rest of us
 were planning

57:18.904 --> 57:20.204
 a long weekend at Key West,

57:20.306 --> 57:24.879
 he was planning an actual
 trip to the actual moon.

57:24.981 --> 57:26.880
JOURNALIST: McArthur,
what do you say to the critics

57:26.982 --> 57:29.917
who see you spending
$50 million to fly to space

57:30.019 --> 57:32.122
when half your employees
don't have health insurance?

57:32.224 --> 57:34.692
Fifty? More like ninety.

57:34.794 --> 57:38.261
Look, if I could do this kind
of thing for cheap, I would.

57:38.363 --> 57:40.529
But it's incredibly expensive.

57:40.631 --> 57:41.861
-Gassed up?
-ASSISTANT: Yes, sir.

57:41.963 --> 57:43.368
MCARTHUR: Spot check?
ASSISTANT: Yes, sir.

57:43.470 --> 57:44.628
MCARTHUR: Where's my coffee,
by the way?

57:44.730 --> 57:45.999
BECKET: Here you go.

57:47.468 --> 57:48.670
Lock and load.

57:48.773 --> 57:50.306
BECKET: All it took
 was a laminated pass

57:50.408 --> 57:51.943
 and a shirt from the mall.

57:52.045 --> 57:54.110
(ALARM BLARING)

57:54.913 --> 57:58.509
MAN: (OVER RADIO) Charlie 17,
 you are very low, over.

57:58.611 --> 57:59.648
(BELL TOLLS)

57:59.750 --> 58:02.880
1,500 square feet,
three bedrooms, doorman.

58:02.982 --> 58:05.390
You ever have
a doorman before?

58:05.492 --> 58:07.120
-I barely had a door.
-(REALTOR CHUCKLES)

58:07.222 --> 58:09.756
REALTOR: It changes your life.
I'm not even joking around.

58:09.858 --> 58:12.591
This is original marble
from, uh, Italy.

58:12.693 --> 58:13.793
And if you look out there,

58:13.895 --> 58:15.699
that's what you pay
the money for.

58:23.002 --> 58:24.235
So would you
want to live here?

58:25.738 --> 58:26.877
(VEHICLE HONKS)

58:26.979 --> 58:27.942
With me?

58:29.877 --> 58:33.750
I know
it's a little fast, but...

58:35.047 --> 58:37.215
I'd really
like to have you here.

58:39.324 --> 58:40.922
I'd love it, actually.

58:42.260 --> 58:43.221
If I'm being honest.

58:46.032 --> 58:46.994
Uh... (CHUCKLES)

58:48.198 --> 58:49.194
Um...

58:50.871 --> 58:51.834
Yeah.

58:52.435 --> 58:53.605
I'd love that too.

58:55.308 --> 58:56.100
Now, I know the place is a lot

58:56.202 --> 58:57.540
but Warren's gonna give me
a bridge loan

58:57.642 --> 58:58.977
and the neighborhood's
appreciating...

58:59.079 --> 59:00.810
RUTH: Hey, hey.

59:00.912 --> 59:03.780
I liked you when you lived
in Newark and took the bus.

59:04.877 --> 59:06.145
You know that, right?

59:09.417 --> 59:10.622
What?

59:15.621 --> 59:16.859
Nothing.

59:16.961 --> 59:21.564
By the way, I can fire you
at any time, but I won't.

59:21.666 --> 59:24.801
-(ALL LAUGHING)
-(STAMMERS, CHUCKLES)

59:24.903 --> 59:28.572
To continue with this story,
and he said, he's, like...

59:28.675 --> 59:29.836
"What are you talking about?
Where are you?"

59:29.938 --> 59:31.610
And I was, like,
"I'm in Highland Park."

59:32.344 --> 59:34.909
He was, like, "No..."

59:35.011 --> 59:37.415
BECKET: As for the next
 Redfellow in line,

59:37.517 --> 59:39.215
 you can probably
 guess who it was.

59:39.317 --> 59:40.311
(WARREN LAUGHS)

59:40.413 --> 59:42.253
BECKET: But by now,
 I couldn't imagine lifting

59:42.355 --> 59:44.420
 a finger against my uncle,

59:44.523 --> 59:46.922
 much less doing the man harm.

59:47.024 --> 59:50.459
And by that point, things were
going decently well.

59:50.561 --> 59:53.632
The job, living situation...

59:55.963 --> 59:57.295
FATHER MORRIS:
You were content.

59:59.738 --> 01:00:02.806
Without the wealth.
Without the inheritance.

01:00:06.210 --> 01:00:07.206
Well...

01:00:08.141 --> 01:00:10.143
 Maybe you're right.
 Maybe I was...

01:00:11.413 --> 01:00:12.409
 content.

01:00:13.285 --> 01:00:14.246
 Content enough.

01:00:16.382 --> 01:00:18.089
 And I suppose I had
 more important things

01:00:18.191 --> 01:00:19.017
 to think about.

01:00:19.119 --> 01:00:21.792
RUTH: My mom's gonna
 want Zinfandel.

01:00:21.894 --> 01:00:23.793
I think we're making
the right choice, by the way.

01:00:23.895 --> 01:00:26.596
Having an engagement party
at your home just feels,

01:00:26.698 --> 01:00:30.097
better than
at a bar or something.

01:00:30.664 --> 01:00:32.968
I totally agree.

01:00:35.367 --> 01:00:37.071
RUTH: I'm still thinking
about your family.

01:00:38.673 --> 01:00:39.876
All the crazy shit.

01:00:40.706 --> 01:00:41.911
Okay.

01:00:42.711 --> 01:00:43.777
I don't mean to obsess,

01:00:43.879 --> 01:00:45.946
but don't you think
that it's...

01:00:46.048 --> 01:00:48.346
BECKET: I'm not even
a part of that family.

01:00:48.448 --> 01:00:50.282
Whatever's going on, it's got
nothing to do with us.

01:00:51.558 --> 01:00:53.153
Besides, it's probably
over anyway.

01:00:54.119 --> 01:00:55.320
RUTH: What makes you say that?

01:00:58.890 --> 01:01:00.260
I don't know.

01:01:00.563 --> 01:01:02.226
Just sayin' it.

01:01:02.329 --> 01:01:04.703
-(TRAFFIC BUSTLING)
-(DISTANT SIRENS BLARING)

01:01:09.202 --> 01:01:11.835
PINFIELD: Excuse me.
Mr. Redfellow?

01:01:11.937 --> 01:01:13.239
Becket Redfellow?

01:01:15.875 --> 01:01:17.078
How you doing today?

01:01:20.716 --> 01:01:21.852
(BECKET CLEARS THROAT)

01:01:24.316 --> 01:01:25.856
MATTHEWS: Nice office
you got here.

01:01:27.591 --> 01:01:29.559
I like it. (CHUCKLES)

01:01:29.661 --> 01:01:30.625
PINFIELD:
Just so we understand,

01:01:30.727 --> 01:01:31.824
you said you're not an heir

01:01:31.927 --> 01:01:33.160
to the estate,
is that correct?

01:01:33.860 --> 01:01:35.566
As far as I know.

01:01:35.668 --> 01:01:38.165
Well, we did
a little research, and...

01:01:39.205 --> 01:01:40.200
Congratulations.

01:01:52.680 --> 01:01:54.285
BECKET: Wow.

01:01:54.387 --> 01:01:56.679
Uh, it's just a little...

01:01:57.048 --> 01:01:58.887
I... I had no idea.

01:01:58.990 --> 01:02:01.556
Hmm. Can you answer
a few questions for us?

01:02:01.658 --> 01:02:02.759
Yeah, I'm... I'm sorry.

01:02:02.861 --> 01:02:04.221
Um, I... I really had no idea.
This is...

01:02:04.323 --> 01:02:05.863
PINFIELD: Nobody's
arguing with you.

01:02:07.359 --> 01:02:08.696
MATTHEWS: Can you tell us
where you were

01:02:08.799 --> 01:02:09.828
on the afternoon
of April 10th?

01:02:09.930 --> 01:02:11.330
It would've been a Sunday.

01:02:15.472 --> 01:02:16.434
BECKET: Oh...

01:02:17.202 --> 01:02:19.742
April 10th. Okay. Here we go.

01:02:19.844 --> 01:02:21.076
MATTHEWS: You're
fucking kidding me.

01:02:22.145 --> 01:02:24.677
He remembers when
and where he bought a hot dog.

01:02:24.779 --> 01:02:26.082
Is that even him?

01:02:26.384 --> 01:02:27.681
I don't know.

01:02:27.783 --> 01:02:28.952
Can you see who it is?

01:02:31.023 --> 01:02:33.524
PINFIELD: I can't see shit.
MATTHEWS: Me neither.

01:02:33.626 --> 01:02:34.959
PINFIELD: All right,
follow him.

01:02:35.061 --> 01:02:37.793
WOMAN: Rothburn's going down,
and Bellman's gonna go too.

01:02:37.895 --> 01:02:39.389
They're minutes away,
I guarantee it.

01:02:39.491 --> 01:02:41.498
MAN: I say we dump
whatever we can cut loose

01:02:41.600 --> 01:02:42.867
before the markets catch wind.

01:02:42.969 --> 01:02:45.837
WOMAN: We can say we were
forced into it, which is true.

01:02:46.435 --> 01:02:47.399
No.

01:02:49.341 --> 01:02:50.300
I spent 35 years

01:02:50.402 --> 01:02:52.569
earning the trust
of these shareholders.

01:02:53.845 --> 01:02:55.312
I'm not throwing them
to the sharks

01:02:55.414 --> 01:02:56.544
in one afternoon.

01:02:56.646 --> 01:02:58.575
(CELLPHONE RINGING)

01:03:00.850 --> 01:03:03.321
-Oh, shit.
-BECKET: What?

01:03:03.423 --> 01:03:04.823
(WARREN EXHALES DEEPLY)

01:03:08.861 --> 01:03:11.324
-Goddamn! (GRUNTING)
-Oh, whoa. Oh, oh, oh!

01:03:14.194 --> 01:03:16.098
-(GASPING)
-MAN: Is he all right?

01:03:18.033 --> 01:03:19.530
-Becket...
-Call an ambulance!

01:03:24.304 --> 01:03:26.405
WARREN: Pass me that water,
 will ya?

01:03:27.512 --> 01:03:29.474
(GRUNTS, GULPING)

01:03:33.517 --> 01:03:35.348
(EXHALES, SIGHS)

01:03:37.257 --> 01:03:38.788
(CHUCKLES)

01:03:38.890 --> 01:03:40.991
Listen, I'm not
gonna mince words.

01:03:44.129 --> 01:03:46.326
You want to chase that rabbit
down the hole, huh?

01:03:47.599 --> 01:03:49.560
Okay. That money rabbit.

01:03:50.999 --> 01:03:52.497
Everybody loves a good chase.

01:03:55.640 --> 01:03:56.875
And you're good at it.

01:03:58.872 --> 01:04:00.208
But here I am,

01:04:01.040 --> 01:04:02.606
61 years old and...

01:04:05.214 --> 01:04:07.479
you're the only visitor
I've had all day.

01:04:11.583 --> 01:04:14.156
Go find that person
in your life, Becket.

01:04:16.692 --> 01:04:17.654
Whoever it is.

01:04:19.465 --> 01:04:20.558
Work at loving them.

01:04:22.996 --> 01:04:24.595
I mean, really work.

01:04:26.998 --> 01:04:28.203
'Cause...

01:04:28.904 --> 01:04:30.139
at the end of the day...

01:04:31.776 --> 01:04:33.307
it's the only job that pays.

01:04:40.045 --> 01:04:42.079
(DUCKS QUACKING)

01:04:42.181 --> 01:04:44.153
(CHORAL MUSIC PLAYING)

01:04:50.424 --> 01:04:51.959
BECKET: It was in this
 unhappy moment

01:04:52.061 --> 01:04:54.295
 that I realized
 an ironic truth.

01:04:56.096 --> 01:04:57.496
 There is only one left.

01:04:59.003 --> 01:05:00.536
MAN: You can either
get rid of it,

01:05:00.638 --> 01:05:02.237
or do what you like.

01:05:05.004 --> 01:05:06.373
But not here.

01:05:08.173 --> 01:05:09.607
Not under this roof.

01:05:13.920 --> 01:05:16.350
And I think you know
I have to stand by that.

01:05:18.755 --> 01:05:20.288
A man of my word.

01:05:21.461 --> 01:05:23.456
BECKET: One left.

01:05:24.556 --> 01:05:26.157
 But what use was it
 to fantasize?

01:05:26.260 --> 01:05:28.764
 I had put all that behind me.

01:05:28.866 --> 01:05:31.266
Hey, Becket. Letter for you.

01:05:32.033 --> 01:05:33.202
-Thanks, Brian.
-Yep.

01:05:41.207 --> 01:05:42.981
(CHORAL MUSIC CONTINUES)

01:05:46.886 --> 01:05:48.415
-(MUSIC STOPS)
-(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

01:05:49.820 --> 01:05:51.522
-Hey.
-He invited me.

01:05:51.624 --> 01:05:52.617
RUTH: (OVER PHONE) What?

01:05:53.460 --> 01:05:55.222
My grandfather.

01:05:55.324 --> 01:05:58.095
To a dinner party
at the estate. (CHUCKLES)

01:05:59.159 --> 01:06:01.163
- Hello?
-Uh, I just...

01:06:01.265 --> 01:06:03.626
I... I thought you said
you would never do that?

01:06:03.729 --> 01:06:05.162
-Never do what?
-RUTH: Never meet the guy.

01:06:05.264 --> 01:06:06.703
 Wait, when is this?

01:06:06.805 --> 01:06:08.671
-Tonight.
- It's Friday.

01:06:08.773 --> 01:06:10.604
-BECKET: I know.
-Friday.

01:06:10.873 --> 01:06:12.272
BECKET: Oh, shit.

01:06:12.375 --> 01:06:16.173
Ruth, I may not have
this opportunity again.

01:06:16.275 --> 01:06:17.410
He never sees anyone.

01:06:17.512 --> 01:06:19.377
RUTH: You may not have
 this opportunity again?

01:06:19.479 --> 01:06:21.114
-I don't know.
- Yeah, you're right.

01:06:21.216 --> 01:06:22.416
So be home by 7:00
or you will miss

01:06:22.518 --> 01:06:25.348
your own fucking engagement
party, like... (SCOFFS)

01:06:25.450 --> 01:06:27.751
Right. Of course. Of course.

01:06:29.054 --> 01:06:30.561
Okay.

01:06:30.663 --> 01:06:32.195
I love you, by the way.

01:06:36.295 --> 01:06:37.497
I'm gonna call you back.

01:06:39.870 --> 01:06:41.567
Package for Mr. Redfellow.

01:06:55.621 --> 01:06:56.582
Remember to breathe.

01:06:57.656 --> 01:06:58.584
Very important.

01:07:00.055 --> 01:07:01.653
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS)

01:07:03.960 --> 01:07:05.393
(UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING)

01:07:07.831 --> 01:07:09.067
Taylor drowned.

01:07:10.268 --> 01:07:12.030
He went to Princeton
on a swimming scholarship

01:07:12.132 --> 01:07:13.533
and he drowned.

01:07:14.833 --> 01:07:17.372
I became more than a bit
suspicious right then.

01:07:18.307 --> 01:07:20.375
So I had a little friend
follow you.

01:07:21.647 --> 01:07:23.114
Aren't those great?

01:07:24.479 --> 01:07:26.183
I'm really happy
I went with black and white.

01:07:27.949 --> 01:07:29.615
(SIGHS DEEPLY)

01:07:32.318 --> 01:07:33.652
(GRUNTS, SLAMS TABLE)

01:07:35.860 --> 01:07:36.853
BECKET: What do you want?

01:07:39.565 --> 01:07:40.659
Finish it.

01:07:42.562 --> 01:07:44.734
I'm under investigation
by the FBI.

01:07:44.836 --> 01:07:46.302
And yet here you are.

01:07:47.269 --> 01:07:48.332
It's almost as if,
I don't know,

01:07:48.434 --> 01:07:49.734
they don't quite have a case.

01:07:51.303 --> 01:07:53.177
Which is bananas.

01:07:55.575 --> 01:07:58.446
Anyway, I will need
a down payment.

01:08:00.018 --> 01:08:02.551
-A what?
-300,000 by five o'clock.

01:08:02.653 --> 01:08:03.447
Shit.

01:08:03.549 --> 01:08:05.048
JULIA: I'm done
fucking around.

01:08:05.150 --> 01:08:06.316
It's...

01:08:06.418 --> 01:08:07.485
You gotta be shitting me.

01:08:07.587 --> 01:08:09.388
You still have a company
checkbook, right?

01:08:09.490 --> 01:08:11.723
You still have access
to the accounts?

01:08:12.625 --> 01:08:14.160
Deliver the cheques
to my husband.

01:08:14.262 --> 01:08:16.099
He's in his office in Hoboken,

01:08:16.202 --> 01:08:17.865
waiting on you like
a patient little puppy.

01:08:17.967 --> 01:08:19.069
You have 30 minutes.

01:08:19.171 --> 01:08:20.364
Any longer than that
and she'll get a package

01:08:20.466 --> 01:08:21.771
just like the one I gave you.

01:08:21.873 --> 01:08:22.800
Who will get a package?

01:08:24.374 --> 01:08:27.111
Your little girlfriend,
who do you think?

01:08:27.213 --> 01:08:29.708
Cardozo High School
in Bayside, Queens, right?

01:08:31.213 --> 01:08:32.711
She's in for quite the shock.

01:08:34.148 --> 01:08:36.251
For what it's worth,

01:08:36.353 --> 01:08:38.156
I was hoping
for a different arrangement.

01:08:40.452 --> 01:08:41.885
Something a bit more fun.

01:08:44.764 --> 01:08:46.164
But you blew it, Becket.

01:08:48.328 --> 01:08:49.893
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:08:51.031 --> 01:08:52.236
Brian.

01:08:53.305 --> 01:08:55.267
Call Fritzer in Vienna.
We're gonna sell P&G.

01:08:55.369 --> 01:08:56.334
Tell him to name his price.

01:08:56.436 --> 01:08:58.543
Call? Am I allowed to do that?

01:08:58.645 --> 01:08:59.571
What? Just do it.

01:08:59.673 --> 01:09:02.477
MATTHEWS: Uh-huh.
I've got him right now.

01:09:04.617 --> 01:09:05.478
Yes, ma'am.

01:09:05.581 --> 01:09:08.252
Headed North on Hanover.
That's North, Hanover.

01:09:16.022 --> 01:09:17.228
Sir?

01:09:17.862 --> 01:09:18.861
Excuse me, sir!

01:09:18.963 --> 01:09:19.956
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

01:09:22.064 --> 01:09:24.301
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

01:09:27.939 --> 01:09:29.867
RECEPTIONIST: Excuse me?

01:09:36.210 --> 01:09:37.309
He's just not here.

01:09:37.411 --> 01:09:38.612
-I don't...
-(DOOR OPENS)

01:09:39.949 --> 01:09:40.977
Is that her?

01:09:41.786 --> 01:09:43.018
Gimme that.

01:09:43.120 --> 01:09:44.888
I'm here. I got your cheques,

01:09:44.991 --> 01:09:48.489
you sociopathic,
conniving bitch.

01:09:48.591 --> 01:09:50.888
Jesus Christ, Becket.
This could've been anyone.

01:09:52.357 --> 01:09:53.658
Call it off.

01:09:53.760 --> 01:09:55.529
Well, just write
the checks first, will you?

01:09:55.631 --> 01:09:56.894
-I want to be positive...
-(RECEIVER CLATTERING)

01:09:59.134 --> 01:10:00.565
Cheer up, Lyle.

01:10:00.667 --> 01:10:01.899
You're about to make
a lot of money.

01:10:02.001 --> 01:10:04.337
LYLE: I'm not gonna make
any money. Are you kidding?

01:10:04.439 --> 01:10:08.077
She's just gonna take it
and leave.

01:10:08.179 --> 01:10:10.314
I'm not the one
she wants anyway.

01:10:12.913 --> 01:10:15.847
But you... you're really
coming up in the world, huh?

01:10:18.650 --> 01:10:21.357
Just... Just a little bastard.

01:10:21.459 --> 01:10:23.756
Just a little bastard
from Newark. (CHUCKLES)

01:10:25.059 --> 01:10:26.158
(SLAPS)

01:10:26.260 --> 01:10:27.496
(LYLE GROANS SOFTLY)

01:10:28.900 --> 01:10:29.828
(BOTH GRUNTING)

01:10:33.771 --> 01:10:36.307
(SOBBING)

01:10:41.107 --> 01:10:43.776
BECKET: I'd already committed
 embezzlement and assault.

01:10:44.882 --> 01:10:46.309
 So fuck it.

01:10:46.411 --> 01:10:47.478
(ELEVATOR DINGS)

01:10:47.580 --> 01:10:48.913
AUTOMATED VOICE: Going down.

01:10:49.547 --> 01:10:51.553
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:10:55.420 --> 01:10:57.625
(RAIN PATTERING)

01:11:06.837 --> 01:11:07.833
(SIGHS)

01:11:17.214 --> 01:11:18.844
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

01:11:27.222 --> 01:11:29.360
(KEYPAD CLICKING)

01:11:32.458 --> 01:11:34.530
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

01:11:36.294 --> 01:11:37.596
Hi!

01:11:37.698 --> 01:11:39.634
How are you?
Thank you for coming.

01:11:42.203 --> 01:11:44.738
(RAIN PATTERING)

01:11:46.276 --> 01:11:48.379
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES)

01:12:07.964 --> 01:12:08.927
(GRUNTS)

01:12:26.951 --> 01:12:28.617
(DOOR SLAMS)

01:12:31.253 --> 01:12:33.853
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:12:55.641 --> 01:12:57.811
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:13:06.623 --> 01:13:09.592
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)
-(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:13:21.139 --> 01:13:22.031
On account of the storm,

01:13:22.133 --> 01:13:25.575
I decided to cancel
the festivities tonight.

01:13:27.841 --> 01:13:30.173
But I just couldn't
turn you down.

01:13:33.885 --> 01:13:35.453
Whitelaw.

01:13:37.089 --> 01:13:38.852
(CLEARS THROAT) Becket.

01:13:40.851 --> 01:13:42.625
Did you bring an appetite?

01:13:43.963 --> 01:13:46.389
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:13:46.491 --> 01:13:47.960
So...

01:13:49.194 --> 01:13:52.195
Been working your way
up the financial ladder.

01:13:53.070 --> 01:13:54.505
Is that right?

01:13:57.074 --> 01:13:57.868
Trying to.

01:13:57.970 --> 01:14:00.511
I understand
you've come a long ways.

01:14:01.412 --> 01:14:03.514
Must've really
put in the hours.

01:14:05.318 --> 01:14:08.178
A filthy business, though,
isn't it?

01:14:09.482 --> 01:14:10.785
How do you mean?

01:14:11.824 --> 01:14:12.886
Come on.

01:14:14.325 --> 01:14:16.186
One professional to another,

01:14:18.591 --> 01:14:20.498
you must have, uh...

01:14:21.066 --> 01:14:23.333
broken a few heads,

01:14:23.435 --> 01:14:26.900
bumped off some of
the competition, no?

01:14:29.074 --> 01:14:30.470
Two or three, maybe.

01:14:30.572 --> 01:14:32.543
Would you take any of it back?

01:14:33.609 --> 01:14:35.678
Because
this sort of life is...

01:14:36.811 --> 01:14:39.242
it isn't cut out for everyone,
is it?

01:14:43.619 --> 01:14:46.249
It would make
some people tired.

01:14:47.485 --> 01:14:48.691
Old.

01:14:50.027 --> 01:14:51.023
Lonely.

01:14:51.997 --> 01:14:53.256
Regretful.

01:14:56.602 --> 01:15:01.066
But me, I've always felt
I know a certain truth,

01:15:02.905 --> 01:15:04.869
that the only thing
that really hurts us in life

01:15:04.971 --> 01:15:07.138
is the voice
of our own conscience...

01:15:08.910 --> 01:15:12.583
telling us a story
about right and wrong.

01:15:13.617 --> 01:15:14.612
And if you know
how to turn your head

01:15:14.714 --> 01:15:16.620
just right into the wind,

01:15:17.887 --> 01:15:20.624
you can make that voice
go down to a whisper.

01:15:23.292 --> 01:15:24.760
After a while...

01:15:27.465 --> 01:15:29.226
you might never hear it
at all.

01:15:32.368 --> 01:15:36.332
(CLOCK CHIMING)

01:15:41.344 --> 01:15:42.646
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

01:15:44.713 --> 01:15:47.013
She was my favorite,
by the way.

01:15:49.848 --> 01:15:52.189
Sharpest of the bunch.

01:15:52.291 --> 01:15:54.224
Always knew what she wanted

01:15:54.326 --> 01:15:55.890
and willing to fight for it.

01:15:58.296 --> 01:15:59.630
Why didn't you help her...

01:16:02.233 --> 01:16:03.359
when she needed it?

01:16:08.971 --> 01:16:11.873
You know where
this is all going, don't you?

01:16:14.573 --> 01:16:16.378
Come on.

01:16:16.480 --> 01:16:18.011
I wanna show you something...

01:16:19.848 --> 01:16:22.653
before Charles
brings out the pudding.

01:16:23.484 --> 01:16:24.688
(DOOR OPENS)

01:16:35.961 --> 01:16:37.899
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

01:16:43.108 --> 01:16:44.235
A trench gun,

01:16:45.103 --> 01:16:47.370
belonged to your
great-great-uncle,

01:16:48.080 --> 01:16:49.372
World War I.

01:16:52.179 --> 01:16:55.011
These... These things
mortified the Germans.

01:16:55.113 --> 01:16:56.816
They'd never seen anything
like it.

01:16:56.918 --> 01:16:58.689
-(GUN COCKING)
-(SHELL CLATTERING)

01:17:04.722 --> 01:17:05.894
Here.

01:17:06.361 --> 01:17:07.665
Go ahead.

01:17:09.265 --> 01:17:10.228
Go ahead.

01:17:13.437 --> 01:17:15.134
Draw a bead on something.

01:17:22.281 --> 01:17:23.439
I want you to try this.

01:17:27.085 --> 01:17:28.213
Here.

01:17:28.780 --> 01:17:30.116
Right here.

01:17:40.165 --> 01:17:41.094
(EXHALES SOFTLY)

01:17:44.698 --> 01:17:46.902
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

01:17:57.810 --> 01:17:59.376
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

01:18:04.685 --> 01:18:05.888
I better be going.

01:18:06.388 --> 01:18:07.384
Where to?

01:18:10.062 --> 01:18:11.058
Home.

01:18:14.299 --> 01:18:15.733
You're almost there.

01:18:20.733 --> 01:18:21.965
(GUN CLICKING)

01:18:22.067 --> 01:18:23.499
WHITELAW: (SIGHING) Well...

01:18:26.577 --> 01:18:28.273
you better go quickly then.

01:18:29.347 --> 01:18:31.045
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:18:41.491 --> 01:18:42.485
(DOORKNOB RATTLING)

01:18:48.728 --> 01:18:49.965
(BECKET SIGHS)

01:18:57.001 --> 01:18:58.468
(DOORKNOB RATTLING)

01:19:08.352 --> 01:19:09.380
(RATTLING)

01:19:11.952 --> 01:19:13.857
(METAL CREAKING IN DISTANCE)

01:19:15.427 --> 01:19:17.861
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:19:26.238 --> 01:19:27.200
(LOCKS CLICKING)

01:19:29.538 --> 01:19:30.533
(DOOR OPENS)

01:19:33.740 --> 01:19:35.274
(SHUDDERS)

01:19:43.555 --> 01:19:45.014
-(GUNSHOT)
-(BECKET YELPS)

01:19:45.116 --> 01:19:46.824
-(GRUNTS)
-(DOOR CLOSES)

01:19:49.053 --> 01:19:50.723
(WHITELAW GROANING)

01:19:50.825 --> 01:19:52.295
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:19:52.397 --> 01:19:53.325
(BOTH GROANING)

01:19:57.502 --> 01:19:58.995
-(SQUELCHING)
-(GRUNTS)

01:19:59.097 --> 01:20:01.033
Go on and fuckin' run!

01:20:01.135 --> 01:20:03.772
Doors are boarded up
from the outside.

01:20:03.874 --> 01:20:05.975
-Charles made sure of that.
-Shit!

01:20:10.046 --> 01:20:12.882
-(GLASS SHATTERING)
-(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

01:20:12.984 --> 01:20:15.281
-(BECKET PANTING)
-WHITELAW: There's no way out!

01:20:15.982 --> 01:20:18.416
Go on. Tire yourself!

01:20:19.283 --> 01:20:21.989
Come to my house to kill me?

01:20:22.091 --> 01:20:23.322
-(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)
-(GLASS SHATTERING)

01:20:23.424 --> 01:20:26.395
You best have done that
when I gave you the chance.

01:20:26.497 --> 01:20:28.459
(GRUNTS, PANTS)

01:20:29.833 --> 01:20:32.166
(BREATHING HEAVILY)
Okay. Okay.

01:20:33.403 --> 01:20:35.103
(PANTING)

01:20:37.739 --> 01:20:40.838
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:20:41.540 --> 01:20:45.679
-(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)
-(BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:20:45.781 --> 01:20:47.876
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:20:47.978 --> 01:20:49.579
(PANTING)

01:20:52.117 --> 01:20:54.316
(BOW SNAPS, CLATTERS)

01:20:54.418 --> 01:20:56.586
-(GUNSHOT)
-(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

01:20:57.889 --> 01:20:59.391
(GUNSHOT)

01:21:00.860 --> 01:21:01.926
(GUN CLICKS)

01:21:02.028 --> 01:21:03.494
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:21:08.103 --> 01:21:09.665
-(GUN COCKING)
-(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

01:21:16.677 --> 01:21:17.679
(GROANS)

01:21:17.781 --> 01:21:19.345
-(BLOOD GUSHING)
-(CHOKING)

01:21:34.530 --> 01:21:35.625
(EXHALES)

01:21:36.897 --> 01:21:39.128
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:21:39.230 --> 01:21:40.936
BECKET: Believe this.

01:21:41.038 --> 01:21:44.238
 My final murder
 was not a murder at all

01:21:44.340 --> 01:21:47.340
 but a perfectly legitimate
 act of self-defense.

01:21:49.547 --> 01:21:50.813
OFFICER: All right.

01:21:50.915 --> 01:21:52.477
Sheriff's Department's
on the way.

01:21:53.385 --> 01:21:54.247
BECKET: Okay.

01:21:54.349 --> 01:21:55.445
OFFICER: They're just gonna
talk to you, okay?

01:21:55.548 --> 01:21:57.917
All right. All right. Um...
(CLEARS THROAT)

01:21:58.019 --> 01:21:59.316
I... I need to... I need to go

01:21:59.418 --> 01:22:01.255
'cause I have
my engagement party.

01:22:02.121 --> 01:22:03.154
 It started an hour ago.

01:22:03.256 --> 01:22:04.460
OFFICER:
 Whose engagement party?

01:22:04.562 --> 01:22:05.454
BECKET: It's mine.

01:22:05.556 --> 01:22:07.464
DETECTIVE: So you had
no relationship

01:22:07.566 --> 01:22:08.698
with your grandfather?

01:22:08.800 --> 01:22:10.964
I'd never met him
before tonight.

01:22:11.066 --> 01:22:14.035
-Not even once?
-BECKET: Never.

01:22:14.137 --> 01:22:15.998
Look, if I'm not
legally required to be here,

01:22:16.100 --> 01:22:17.773
I need to leave.

01:22:17.875 --> 01:22:19.105
You're not
legally required to,

01:22:19.207 --> 01:22:21.244
but, uh...
I'd prefer if you stay.

01:22:21.346 --> 01:22:22.276
Okay.

01:22:23.207 --> 01:22:24.377
(CAR ALARM CHIRPING)

01:22:25.682 --> 01:22:27.116
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

01:22:38.157 --> 01:22:40.063
-(SIGHS)
-(DOOR OPENS)

01:22:41.028 --> 01:22:43.027
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:22:43.129 --> 01:22:44.562
(BECKET SIGHS SOFTLY)

01:22:48.736 --> 01:22:49.732
(SIGHING)

01:22:51.673 --> 01:22:52.702
(EXHALES)

01:23:00.050 --> 01:23:01.213
I'll give you
the full explanation.

01:23:01.315 --> 01:23:03.086
You're withholding
something from me.

01:23:04.286 --> 01:23:06.485
You've been withholding
something from me.

01:23:07.458 --> 01:23:08.687
(SIGHS)

01:23:08.956 --> 01:23:10.324
So right now...

01:23:12.325 --> 01:23:14.097
you have to tell me
what's up...

01:23:15.566 --> 01:23:16.528
or I'm out.

01:23:22.869 --> 01:23:24.041
(EXHALES)

01:23:28.941 --> 01:23:30.206
(SIGHS)

01:23:30.308 --> 01:23:32.511
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

01:23:38.983 --> 01:23:42.452
BECKET: Sometimes in life,
 you gotta take a deep breath,

01:23:42.554 --> 01:23:45.095
 come clean
 to the person you love.

01:23:48.098 --> 01:23:51.562
 This was not
 one of those times.

01:23:51.664 --> 01:23:53.334
 I only told her
 what she'd see on the news.

01:23:53.436 --> 01:23:55.101
NEWS REPORTER: ... is indeed
 dead, and it seems...

01:23:55.203 --> 01:23:56.303
BECKET:
 My grandfather was gone.

01:23:56.405 --> 01:23:57.906
NEWS REPORTER:
 ...some sort of altercation...

01:23:58.008 --> 01:23:59.703
BECKET:
 And as for the fortune,

01:24:00.742 --> 01:24:01.710
 well...

01:24:01.812 --> 01:24:03.542
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

01:24:17.990 --> 01:24:19.195
(SIGHS)

01:24:24.201 --> 01:24:26.532
-(ALL APPLAUDING)
-(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

01:24:51.292 --> 01:24:52.756
BECKET: The right kind
 of life.

01:24:53.557 --> 01:24:55.396
 This had to be it, right?

01:24:57.464 --> 01:24:58.933
 Sure, she had
 a few misgivings,

01:24:59.036 --> 01:25:01.600
 but we can handle that later.

01:25:03.137 --> 01:25:06.136
 For now, I was rich.

01:25:06.238 --> 01:25:08.241
 And being rich

01:25:08.343 --> 01:25:10.675
 is even better
 than you imagine.

01:25:11.914 --> 01:25:13.612
(MUSIC CONCLUDES)

01:25:16.952 --> 01:25:19.618
(CLOCK TICKING)

01:25:20.918 --> 01:25:23.721
You know I mentioned earlier,
this is a tragedy.

01:25:26.025 --> 01:25:27.230
Still is.

01:25:28.363 --> 01:25:30.461
-Donald Macnamara, my wife.
-Hello.

01:25:30.563 --> 01:25:31.766
-Such a pleasure.
-Nice to meet you.

01:25:31.868 --> 01:25:33.531
Nice to meet you.

01:25:33.633 --> 01:25:36.939
-RUTH: Hi.
-Nancy Dillard, the Dillards.

01:25:37.041 --> 01:25:38.406
-Nice to meet you.
-NANCY: Mmm-hmm.

01:25:39.106 --> 01:25:40.376
Megan Pinfield.

01:25:40.478 --> 01:25:41.541
FBI.

01:25:42.274 --> 01:25:43.576
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

01:25:44.813 --> 01:25:45.743
Hello.

01:25:49.715 --> 01:25:51.749
Can you shut that door
behind you, please?

01:25:53.317 --> 01:25:54.488
(BECKET SIGHS)

01:25:57.623 --> 01:26:01.357
Look, not to be uncouth,
but this is...

01:26:01.459 --> 01:26:02.457
heroically bad timing.

01:26:02.559 --> 01:26:04.066
Yeah, you're under arrest.

01:26:04.168 --> 01:26:05.563
I need you to stay calm
and cooperate.

01:26:05.665 --> 01:26:08.931
-I'm under arrest? For what?
-For murder.

01:26:11.543 --> 01:26:12.605
Of who?

01:26:13.942 --> 01:26:15.344
Lyle Archdale.

01:26:16.848 --> 01:26:19.282
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

01:26:24.482 --> 01:26:25.651
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

01:26:29.089 --> 01:26:30.656
RUTH: Hey, wait!

01:26:32.456 --> 01:26:34.396
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

01:26:35.866 --> 01:26:37.267
RUTH: What do we do?

01:26:37.834 --> 01:26:38.796
What do we do?

01:26:39.671 --> 01:26:40.930
(ENGINE ROARING)

01:26:41.839 --> 01:26:43.273
Ruth, I love...

01:26:45.040 --> 01:26:47.277
(MUSIC CONTINUES)

01:27:01.157 --> 01:27:02.622
BECKET: Can you believe it?

01:27:04.026 --> 01:27:05.295
 After all this,

01:27:05.397 --> 01:27:07.055
 I'd go down for a killing
 I didn't even commit.

01:27:07.157 --> 01:27:08.528
NEWS REPORTER: Now we wanna
 point out to listeners

01:27:08.630 --> 01:27:11.060
 that Becket Redfellow
 crossed state lines,

01:27:11.162 --> 01:27:13.831
 which is why his trial
 is unfolding in federal court

01:27:13.933 --> 01:27:16.466
 where murder can still mean
 capital punishment

01:27:16.568 --> 01:27:18.801
 for citizens of New Jersey.

01:27:18.903 --> 01:27:22.375
As we can see
from these security tapes,

01:27:22.477 --> 01:27:24.309
Mr. Redfellow
burst into the office

01:27:24.411 --> 01:27:26.742
at approximately 5:03 p.m.,

01:27:26.844 --> 01:27:29.845
and then emerged
just four minutes later,

01:27:29.948 --> 01:27:31.920
which is consistent
with the estimated time

01:27:32.022 --> 01:27:33.653
of Mr. Archdale's death.

01:27:34.587 --> 01:27:37.389
Now, we've heard
from the coroner

01:27:37.491 --> 01:27:39.191
that he estimates
the time of death

01:27:39.293 --> 01:27:41.760
between 5:06 and 5:15 p.m.

01:27:42.262 --> 01:27:43.231
And we've heard

01:27:43.333 --> 01:27:44.826
from the eyewitness
in the hallway,

01:27:44.928 --> 01:27:48.470
who positively identifies
Mr. Redfellow.

01:27:48.572 --> 01:27:51.139
Sir, can you confirm that
this is the murder weapon?

01:27:51.241 --> 01:27:53.473
Uh, I can confirm
that it is, yes.

01:27:53.575 --> 01:27:54.503
And did you find
the defendant's fingerprints

01:27:54.605 --> 01:27:55.637
on the murder weapon?

01:27:55.740 --> 01:27:57.040
FORENSICS EXPERT:
I did, yes.

01:27:57.142 --> 01:28:00.016
How certain are you that, uh,
these are his fingerprints?

01:28:00.118 --> 01:28:01.114
FORENSICS EXPERT:
I'm 100% certain.

01:28:01.216 --> 01:28:02.385
BECKET: A letter opener.

01:28:05.521 --> 01:28:08.491
My entire life
because of a letter opener.

01:28:08.593 --> 01:28:11.592
PROSECUTOR: You were the first
to find your husband's body.

01:28:12.060 --> 01:28:13.188
Is that correct?

01:28:13.290 --> 01:28:14.893
Yes.

01:28:14.995 --> 01:28:18.965
Tell me. Were you in love with
Mr. Redfellow at the time?

01:28:19.067 --> 01:28:20.062
(JULIA SNIFFLES)

01:28:21.168 --> 01:28:22.664
Yes. (CRYING)

01:28:22.766 --> 01:28:24.671
PROSECUTOR:
And he with you?

01:28:30.644 --> 01:28:33.275
Becket Redfellow
has been in love with me

01:28:33.711 --> 01:28:36.045
his entire life. (SNIFFLES)

01:28:36.888 --> 01:28:37.981
(JULIA SOBBING)

01:28:38.083 --> 01:28:40.986
I just never thought he would
do something like this.

01:28:41.088 --> 01:28:43.052
(SOBBING)

01:28:44.290 --> 01:28:45.593
I'm sorry.

01:28:46.693 --> 01:28:48.365
JUDGE: Will the defense
 please rise?

01:28:50.396 --> 01:28:51.499
Upon the verdict,

01:28:51.601 --> 01:28:54.335
the jury finds the defendant,
Becket Redfellow,

01:28:54.437 --> 01:28:56.665
guilty of murder
in the first degree

01:28:56.767 --> 01:28:58.173
as charged in the indictment

01:28:58.275 --> 01:28:59.506
and that
the punishment of death

01:28:59.609 --> 01:29:00.772
-shall be imposed.
-(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

01:29:00.874 --> 01:29:03.011
JUDGE: May the sentence
be recorded by the clerk.

01:29:03.113 --> 01:29:04.812
May God rest his soul.

01:29:04.915 --> 01:29:06.111
Thank you.

01:29:06.213 --> 01:29:07.549
(GAVEL BANGS)

01:29:08.849 --> 01:29:10.748
BECKET: I wish I could find
 the right words

01:29:10.850 --> 01:29:12.950
 to describe this juncture
 in my story.

01:29:14.518 --> 01:29:16.151
(DOOR BUZZING)

01:29:16.828 --> 01:29:17.719
(DOOR SLAMS)

01:29:17.821 --> 01:29:20.089
PRISON GUARD: Cell 15, secure!

01:29:23.896 --> 01:29:26.062
BECKET: But there are
 no right words.

01:29:28.300 --> 01:29:29.300
(EXHALES)

01:29:29.402 --> 01:29:30.770
 There's only time.

01:29:32.739 --> 01:29:34.873
 -And silence.
 - (CLOCK TICKING)

01:29:36.948 --> 01:29:38.910
(CLOCK TICKING)

01:29:44.187 --> 01:29:46.148
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:29:51.291 --> 01:29:52.690
(FOOTSTEPS HALT)

01:29:52.792 --> 01:29:54.061
-PRISON GUARD: Yo.
-(THUMPING ON RAILS)

01:29:54.163 --> 01:29:55.960
You got a visitor.

01:30:05.739 --> 01:30:07.609
PRISON GUARD:
You got three minutes.

01:30:08.913 --> 01:30:09.908
(BECKET SIGHS)

01:30:23.454 --> 01:30:24.626
(INHALES)

01:30:26.827 --> 01:30:29.499
You must be quite the catch
back there.

01:30:35.372 --> 01:30:37.067
You got a big day
coming up, huh?

01:30:39.742 --> 01:30:42.105
You remember that game
we used to play as kids?

01:30:43.378 --> 01:30:44.976
I'd have a secret, and...

01:30:45.943 --> 01:30:46.975
you'd try to guess
what it was.

01:30:47.077 --> 01:30:48.617
If you've got
something to say, say it.

01:30:51.322 --> 01:30:53.017
All right.
I'll give you a hint.

01:30:54.084 --> 01:30:56.625
-It involves handwriting.
-You're foul.

01:30:58.660 --> 01:31:01.223
You're a lump of coal
with makeup.

01:31:03.566 --> 01:31:05.733
I'd rather die in here
than be with you.

01:31:08.569 --> 01:31:10.071
I'll give you another hint.

01:31:10.173 --> 01:31:11.266
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

01:31:12.844 --> 01:31:13.807
Lyle...

01:31:15.378 --> 01:31:17.107
when I found him like that...

01:31:18.711 --> 01:31:20.781
I found something else, too.

01:31:21.650 --> 01:31:23.412
And beautifully written,
I might add.

01:31:23.781 --> 01:31:24.783
What's with the white?

01:31:24.885 --> 01:31:26.550
Are you boys playing doctor
back there?

01:31:26.652 --> 01:31:27.953
Did Lyle leave a note?

01:31:28.055 --> 01:31:30.725
Is that what you're saying?
Did Lyle leave a note?

01:31:32.189 --> 01:31:33.729
-JULIA: You know...
-If Lyle wrote a note...

01:31:33.831 --> 01:31:35.231
-I think I might just leave...
-If that's what you're saying,

01:31:35.333 --> 01:31:36.329
in the name
of all things holy,

01:31:36.431 --> 01:31:37.699
you have to release it.

01:31:40.297 --> 01:31:42.037
-Oh, now you want to talk?
-What do you want?

01:31:42.139 --> 01:31:43.601
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

01:31:43.704 --> 01:31:46.001
-What do you want?
-Becket...

01:31:46.103 --> 01:31:48.303
What could you possibly have
to offer?

01:31:49.514 --> 01:31:51.975
No, no, no, no, no!
Hey, hey, hey! Stop!

01:31:52.078 --> 01:31:54.445
-That's it! (GRUNTING)
-Tell me! Stop! Stop!

01:31:54.547 --> 01:31:55.812
I have 30 seconds!

01:31:55.914 --> 01:31:57.449
-PRISON GUARD: You got 25.
-Okay.

01:31:57.551 --> 01:31:59.882
-Sit down.
-Julia!

01:31:59.984 --> 01:32:02.057
Julia, come here, please!
Please!

01:32:02.159 --> 01:32:03.725
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:32:06.931 --> 01:32:07.894
Okay.

01:32:12.763 --> 01:32:13.966
What do you want?

01:32:19.037 --> 01:32:20.907
-Just give me a moment.
-(SLAMS FIST)

01:32:23.379 --> 01:32:25.076
I'm gonna die in 24 hours.

01:32:25.844 --> 01:32:27.108
You don't want that to happen.

01:32:27.210 --> 01:32:29.278
I know you don't want that
to happen.

01:32:30.814 --> 01:32:32.985
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:32:36.622 --> 01:32:37.957
Give me everything.

01:32:40.961 --> 01:32:42.929
-Sign it over to...
-(LINE DISCONNECTS)

01:32:56.279 --> 01:32:57.979
(ALARM BUZZING)

01:32:58.081 --> 01:32:59.209
(THUDS)

01:33:03.614 --> 01:33:05.116
(EXHALES)

01:33:11.793 --> 01:33:13.696
PRISON GUARD:
You need anything else?

01:33:15.363 --> 01:33:16.864
Got a priest?

01:33:19.436 --> 01:33:21.231
Well, that was some hours ago.

01:33:22.636 --> 01:33:23.703
And if you're curious

01:33:23.805 --> 01:33:27.607
why I've been so calm
and self-assured

01:33:27.709 --> 01:33:29.811
for a man
set to be executed in...

01:33:33.180 --> 01:33:37.379
it's because I thought
our friend Julia, might, uh...

01:33:39.918 --> 01:33:42.384
might come through in the end.

01:33:43.654 --> 01:33:44.892
(INHALES)

01:33:49.630 --> 01:33:50.931
I wonder if she's coming.

01:34:01.843 --> 01:34:03.638
FATHER MORRIS:
"The Lord is my shepherd

01:34:03.940 --> 01:34:05.308
"I shall not want.

01:34:06.310 --> 01:34:09.114
"He maketh me to lie down
in green pastures.

01:34:10.148 --> 01:34:12.617
"He leadeth me
beside the still waters."

01:34:12.719 --> 01:34:14.190
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

01:34:14.292 --> 01:34:16.724
"He restoreth my soul.

01:34:16.827 --> 01:34:18.623
"He leadeth me
in the paths of righteousness

01:34:18.725 --> 01:34:20.191
"for his name's sake.

01:34:21.091 --> 01:34:22.124
"Yea, though I walk through

01:34:22.226 --> 01:34:23.627
"the valley
of the shadow of death

01:34:23.729 --> 01:34:25.460
"I will fear no evil

01:34:26.304 --> 01:34:27.704
"for thou art with me.

01:34:28.771 --> 01:34:31.470
"Thy rod and thy staff
they comfort me."

01:34:31.572 --> 01:34:32.640
(CLOCK TICKING)

01:34:32.742 --> 01:34:36.405
(FATHER MORRIS CONTINUES
INDISTINCTLY)

01:34:38.712 --> 01:34:40.013
PRISON GUARD: Redfellow.

01:34:41.685 --> 01:34:43.720
You're not gonna
fuckin' believe this.

01:34:45.323 --> 01:34:46.885
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

01:34:46.987 --> 01:34:48.119
POLICE CHIEF:
First and foremost,

01:34:48.221 --> 01:34:50.919
we have absolute faith
in our forensic team...

01:34:51.021 --> 01:34:54.830
(CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)

01:35:01.372 --> 01:35:02.365
PRISON GUARD: Open 15.

01:35:02.966 --> 01:35:04.534
(DOOR SLIDING OPEN)

01:35:04.636 --> 01:35:05.841
Let's go.

01:35:08.709 --> 01:35:10.945
(DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES)

01:35:14.680 --> 01:35:15.851
(RUSTLING)

01:35:16.484 --> 01:35:18.513
(DOOR BUZZING)

01:35:32.632 --> 01:35:33.902
(SIGHS SOFTLY)

01:35:46.645 --> 01:35:47.850
(SIGHS)

01:35:48.451 --> 01:35:49.412
BECKET: You came.

01:36:01.093 --> 01:36:02.832
(CAR DOOR CLOSES,
ENGINE STARTS)

01:36:04.698 --> 01:36:05.961
(TIRES SCREECHING)

01:36:06.063 --> 01:36:07.837
(ENGINE ACCELERATING)

01:36:22.848 --> 01:36:24.381
(SIGHS HEAVILY)

01:36:36.830 --> 01:36:37.825
(LATIN POP MUSIC PLAYING)

01:36:37.927 --> 01:36:39.099
(SIGHS)

01:36:46.375 --> 01:36:47.371
(SIGHS)

01:36:50.776 --> 01:36:52.013
All right.

